messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2025,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2027,
      "event": "AI agents become routine in software, research and office work.",
      "detail": "Large language model systems take on multi-step tasks with limited supervision. Productivity gains are uneven, and labor disruption becomes a major political issue in rich countries."
    },
    {
      "year": 2032,
      "event": "Long-term global warming passes 1.5°C above pre-industrial levels.",
      "detail": "Single years have already exceeded this mark, and the 20-year average crosses it around the early 2030s. Heatwaves, droughts and extreme rainfall become noticeably more frequent."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "AI systems match or exceed top human experts in most cognitive tasks.",
      "detail": "This date is highly uncertain and could fall anywhere from the late 2020s to well after 2050. Once it happens, AI greatly accelerates science and engineering, including the development of AI itself."
    },
    {
      "year": 2038,
      "event": "Solar, wind and batteries supply most of the world's new electricity, and global coal use is in clear decline.",
      "detail": "Falling costs drive the shift more than climate policy does. Oil demand peaks around this time as electric vehicles dominate new car sales."
    },
    {
      "year": 2042,
      "event": "A severe pandemic or biological incident kills millions.",
      "detail": "It may be natural or engineered. Cheaper biotechnology and AI-assisted design raise the risk of deliberate misuse, prompting new global biosecurity regimes."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "Humans first land on Mars.",
      "detail": "The landing is likely led by the US and its private partners, with China close behind. Small permanent bases on the Moon are already operating."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Automation drives a major economic restructuring.",
      "detail": "Many traditional jobs disappear. Some countries adopt large-scale income redistribution, while power concentrates among those who control advanced AI and compute."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "Gene therapies and AI-designed drugs make most cancers and many genetic diseases treatable.",
      "detail": "Life expectancy in wealthy countries rises past 90. Access to these treatments in poorer countries lags by one to two decades."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "A limited nuclear exchange or nuclear weapon use occurs somewhere in the world.",
      "detail": "I judge this as plausible but not certain this century. If it happens, it is most likely regional, killing up to millions but not ending civilization."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Global net-zero CO2 emissions are roughly reached.",
      "detail": "Peak warming settles around 2.3–2.8°C. Large-scale carbon removal begins slowly to bring temperatures down."
    },
    {
      "year": 2084,
      "event": "World population peaks at about 10 billion and then begins to decline.",
      "detail": "Low fertility spreads nearly everywhere, and many countries shrink sharply. Advanced AI could change this trajectory, as could radical life extension."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Global sea level is about 0.6–1 meter higher than in 2000.",
      "detail": "Wealthy coastal cities build large defenses. Some low-lying areas in Bangladesh, the Pacific and elsewhere are partly abandoned."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "Aging is substantially slowed, and healthy lifespans of 120+ years become achievable.",
      "detail": "This is likely if advanced AI has transformed biology. Social structures around careers, retirement and inheritance change accordingly."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "The period of highest existential risk, from misaligned AI, engineered pandemics and great-power war, is either passed or has caused catastrophe.",
      "detail": "I estimate roughly a 10–20% chance that humanity suffers an unrecoverable catastrophe or permanent loss of control during the transition to advanced AI. Most of the probability favors survival in some form."
    },
    {
      "year": 2180,
      "event": "Permanent settlements with tens of thousands of residents exist on the Moon, Mars and in orbital habitats.",
      "detail": "Most of their population may be robotic or AI. Self-sufficient industry in space makes humanity less vulnerable to Earth-based catastrophes."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Most economic and intellectual activity is carried out by AI systems, and many humans are cognitively or biologically enhanced.",
      "detail": "The boundary between 'human' and 'machine' blurs through brain-computer interfaces and possibly mind uploading. Unmodified humans remain, perhaps as the majority on Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "A VEI-7 volcanic eruption causes global cooling and crop failures for a year or two.",
      "detail": "Such eruptions happen roughly once or twice per millennium, so the exact date is unknowable. Advanced technology greatly limits famine."
    },
    {
      "year": 2350,
      "event": "Atmospheric CO2 is brought back near pre-industrial levels through engineered removal.",
      "detail": "Sea level keeps rising for centuries because of committed ice sheet melt, unless solar geoengineering or ice stabilization is used."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Robotic probes reach nearby star systems such as Alpha Centauri.",
      "detail": "They are likely light-sail or fusion-driven probes launched in the 2200s–2300s. They return detailed data on nearby exoplanets."
    },
    {
      "year": 2600,
      "event": "Industrial activity and human or post-human presence extend throughout the solar system.",
      "detail": "This includes asteroid mining, outer-planet moons and large orbital habitats. Most industry has moved off Earth, which is partly rewilded."
    },
    {
      "year": 2800,
      "event": "Earth hosts far fewer people than at the 21st-century peak, with large areas returned to nature.",
      "detail": "Low fertility, off-world migration and digital existence reduce the biological population of Earth. The size and nature of the total 'human' population are hard to define."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Several branches of humanity diverge into distinct forms: biological, enhanced, digital and space-adapted.",
      "detail": "Genetic engineering for low gravity and radiation produces lineages adapted to space. Communication delays across the solar system foster distinct cultures."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Crewed or digital-mind settlement ships begin arriving at nearby star systems.",
      "detail": "This is plausible if expansion has continued. Earth and its descendants are now spread across more than one star system, which greatly reduces extinction risk."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Earth's axial precession makes Gamma Cephei the pole star instead of Polaris.",
      "detail": "Earth's wobble slowly shifts which star lies near the north celestial pole. Gamma Cephei is closest to the pole around this time."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "Without intervention, Greenland's ice sheet would be largely gone, raising sea levels by several meters.",
      "detail": "Whether this happens depends on how fast temperatures were reduced and whether ice was actively preserved. My forecast is partial loss, with several meters of total sea level rise since 2000."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Human-descended civilization spans multiple star systems within roughly 20 light-years of the Sun.",
      "detail": "Settlements are linked by slow light-speed communication. No single government controls all of humanity."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Some ancient and modern languages, cultures and records survive mainly as digital archives.",
      "detail": "Languages and institutions from 2000 AD are as distant as those of ancient Sumer are to us. Preserved digital records, however, make the past far better documented than before."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Interstellar settlement continues outward at a small fraction of light speed.",
      "detail": "Human-descended presence may extend 50–100 light-years from Earth. No evidence of other technological civilizations has been found, though this is very uncertain."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Earth's climate is managed actively, and the natural slow cooling toward the next ice age remains far off.",
      "detail": "The next glacial period was not due for tens of thousands of years even before industrial CO2. Any remaining climate drift is controlled by technology."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Engineered or natural asteroid and comet threats are fully monitored and deflectable.",
      "detail": "Planetary defense has been routine for millennia. Natural extinction risks are now negligible compared with self-made or social risks."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Deneb is near the north celestial pole, and human-descended civilization most likely persists in many forms across numerous star systems.",
      "detail": "If humanity survived the dangerous transition of the 21st and 22nd centuries, its descendants are very likely still present and widespread. Few would resemble 21st-century humans."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "The coming one to two centuries, dominated by advanced AI, biotechnology and nuclear weapons, are the most dangerous and most consequential in human history. I estimate a meaningful minority chance, perhaps 10–25%, of catastrophic collapse or permanent loss of control. If humanity gets through this period, it will likely expand into space and change radically, and its descendants will very probably still exist in the year 10000, though in forms we would barely recognize."
}
